WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.680
There are more Transformers out there than&nbsp;
meets the eye. But which one packs the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.760
biggest punch? Here are the top picks for&nbsp;
the most powerful Transformers out there.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.740
Arcee has popped up in many incarnations over&nbsp;
the decades since her initial appearance in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:18.360
1986's "The Transformers: The Movie," making&nbsp;
her one of the more difficult characters to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:22.980
track without flying fully off the rails.&nbsp;
Noting how complicated its chronology can be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.660
Hasbro launched an attempt at bringing various&nbsp;
takes on "Transformers" together under a shared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:32.820
continuity in 2010. This soft reboot saw&nbsp;
what is perhaps the most definitive take on&nbsp;

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.600
Arcee in "Transformers: Prime," where&nbsp;
fans saw her stepping into more of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.200
main character role for the first&nbsp;
two seasons. As that take on Arcee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.500
blended a few details from the past&nbsp;
and reimagined her in other ways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.640
it seems likely that will be the basis&nbsp;
of her character in "Rise of the Beasts."

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.140
Arcee is considered one of the least physically&nbsp;
intimidating Transformers, but her intense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:56.760
willpower makes her one of Optimus Prime's&nbsp;
most trusted allies. In the "Prime" series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:01.980
Arcee can transform into a blue motorcycle,&nbsp;
projecting a hologram named "Sadie" as the driver&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:07.620
to be less easily identifiable by humans and&nbsp;
Decepticons. She can turn her hands into blades&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:11.880
or blasters like many of her fellow Autobots,&nbsp;
but her greatest strength might be the ability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:16.920
to achieve great things under pressure. Having&nbsp;
lost friends in battle before, she's committed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:22.500
to making sure it never happens again, and that&nbsp;
resolve is what makes her such a formidable foe.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.220
Another character hailing from the first&nbsp;
generation of Autobots, the original form&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:30.780
of Mirage was a bit different than the one in&nbsp;
"Transformers: Rise of the Beasts." Although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:35.400
he's undergone several iterations at this point,&nbsp;
he remains one of the most complicated Autobots.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.600
Coming from wealth, he joined the group in&nbsp;
the fight against the Decepticons but has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.500
long-held sympathies across the board.&nbsp;
Despite knowing that the Decepticons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:48.300
are wrong and must be stopped, he likewise&nbsp;
disagrees with the methods of the Autobots.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.980
It makes him a bit of a wild card. With an&nbsp;
arrogant but charming demeanor to top it all off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:56.400
he remains one of the most interesting&nbsp;
characters in Transformers' history.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:02.820
Along with that unique personality, Mirage has a&nbsp;
highly individualized skillset. Per his namesake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:06.780
he can cast projections of himself&nbsp;
to confuse enemies. He also has the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:11.820
ability to turn invisible and even emulate&nbsp;
other Autobots. Mirage previously appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:15.900
in the form of a Ferrari 458, but for&nbsp;
"Rise of the Beasts," he's a Porsche.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.980
Though this design harkens back to prior&nbsp;
incarnations, it is worth noting that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:24.780
fellow Autobot Jazz was the one designed after&nbsp;
a Porsche. Whether this means the film franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:28.800
will be merging these two fan favorites, or has&nbsp;
more to do with behind-the-scenes technicalities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.780
is unclear. Regardless, Mirage's subterfuge&nbsp;
makes him a powerful asset to the Autobots.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:38.280
Eagle-eyed viewers might have noticed a&nbsp;
lightning-fast glimpse of Nightbird in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:42.480
the "Transformers: Rise of the Beasts" trailer.&nbsp;
Appearing in only one episode of the original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:47.760
cartoon, this is the kind of deep-cut they live&nbsp;
to spot. "Enter the Nightbird" introduced viewers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.500
to Doctor Fujiyama, who created Nightbird for the&nbsp;
dubious purpose of proving how great technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:57.960
is and how helpful it can be to humanity. The&nbsp;
cartoon showed surprising foresight by explaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:02.640
that this "helpful" tech was immediately&nbsp;
hijacked by Decepticons and used for evil.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:07.260
Though the Autobots ultimately defeat her, she&nbsp;
remains in stasis, returning for "Universe:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:11.760
The Wreckers" and other brief appearances&nbsp;
down the line, particularly in the IDW comics.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:15.240
While some might assume that there will&nbsp;
be changes in Nightbird's origin with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:18.660
new take on the character, it'll be hard&nbsp;
to improve much on the perfect concept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:24.360
of a ninja robot bent on destruction. Not a&nbsp;
Decepticon or an Autobot but simply a robot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:28.500
programmed with the skills of a ninja, most of&nbsp;
Nightbird's abilities lie in her hand-to-hand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:32.880
combat skills. Besides the throwing stars,&nbsp;
she also wields a powerful beam katana.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:38.220
This grizzled weapons expert of the Autobots is&nbsp;
one of the franchise's longest-running characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:42.600
dating back to that opening three-parter,&nbsp;
"More Than Meets the Eye." One of Optimus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.800
Prime's oldest friends, his tenacity has&nbsp;
seen him survive countless conflicts.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:51.240
More to the point and gruff than the others,&nbsp;
it would be easy to dismiss him as a curmudgeon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:55.500
if he wasn't a true softie at heart. He's a&nbsp;
fan favorite who has shown up in just about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:59.760
every "Transformers" adaptation to date,&nbsp;
adding a serious dose of down-to-earth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.840
mentality to the crew. Though his specific&nbsp;
continuity has shifted over the decades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:08.520
he remains one of the tried and true believers&nbsp;
in Optimus Prime's fight against the Decepticons.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:12.780
"Let's blast their tail rudders out of there."

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:16.020
Though Ironhide might not be the&nbsp;
most powerful in a direct attack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:21.000
he is the go-to of the Autobots when it comes&nbsp;
to protection. Sporting Trithyllium-steel skin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:25.440
that makes him essentially invulnerable, he&nbsp;
often serves as the bodyguard of Optimus Prime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.380
stepping in to deflect attacks&nbsp;
while the others leap into action.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:33.060
He is equipped for battle with a special gun,&nbsp;
which can blast targets with any kind of liquid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:36.600
favoring liquid nitrogen. Still,&nbsp;
there is little denying that his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:40.500
greatest strength is an inability to call it&nbsp;
quits, regardless of what challenges arise.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:44.460
Bumblebee not rating higher on&nbsp;
this list might seem like a snub,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:48.480
but it's not. The character has survived a&nbsp;
franchise that a lot of characters haven't,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:52.800
so this entry is made with the utmost&nbsp;
respect to 'Bee. What he lacks in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:57.300
overwhelming strength of characters like Optimus&nbsp;
Prime, he makes up for in sheer determination,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:01.260
which has shown him capable of&nbsp;
overpowering much stronger foes.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:05.580
Appearing early on with the first generation&nbsp;
of "Transformers" characters, he has long been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:09.840
considered the heart of the Autobots, making&nbsp;
him indispensable for the group's morale in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:14.760
ways that would be difficult to quantify. There's&nbsp;
no denying that his ability to stay optimistic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:19.380
even in the most upsetting of situations, is&nbsp;
practically a superpower in and of itself.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:25.080
"Optimus Prime, I know you're&nbsp;
not evil! I believe in you!"

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:28.620
While he first appeared in the form&nbsp;
of an adorable yellow Volkswagon Bug,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:33.420
he's been redesigned to incorporate more of a&nbsp;
muscle car look, now appearing as a yellow Camaro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:38.460
with bee-like racing stripes. He has many of the&nbsp;
same basic weapons as the other Transformers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:43.440
including body separation abilities, an energy&nbsp;
shield, plasma rifles, and rockets. Yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:48.360
Bumblebee's true power comes from within. While&nbsp;
his upbeat attitude is infectious among the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:52.980
occasionally dour Autobots, Bumblebee is just as&nbsp;
determined as the rest of them on the battlefield.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.275 --> 00:05:58.015
They have regularly relied on his scouting&nbsp;
abilities, as well as his superior marksmanship.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:01.500
All of the major Decepticons are&nbsp;
powerful, including heavy hitters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:05.820
like Lockdown and Soundwave. At the top of&nbsp;
Megatron's list of cronies is Shockwave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:08.940
one of the main antagonists&nbsp;
of 2011's "Dark of the Moon."

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:14.700
Rumored to be capable of defeating even Megatron&nbsp;
in combat, this deadly scientist creates a cult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:19.380
of personality. He gains followers like "The&nbsp;
Last Knight" villain Nitro Zeus who commits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:25.440
acts of terror in his name even after his demise..&nbsp;
Ultimately, his body was used by KSI to create the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:30.960
less-intimidating but still scary Two-Head, who&nbsp;
died via hand grenade. That's probably the last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:35.160
we'll see Shockwave, but at this point, his&nbsp;
resilience is a superpower in and of itself.

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:40.200
Though his adherence to "logic" is a built-in&nbsp;
character flaw that leads to his undoing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:45.840
his misdeeds have had surprising longevity in the&nbsp;
franchise. Shockwave's ability to influence others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:50.400
is put into play at various times, including when&nbsp;
he uses his powers to create subservient clones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:55.500
of himself to fight for him during battles.&nbsp;
He can transform into a tank, redirect blasts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:59.640
by opening portals, and fight Autobots to&nbsp;
a standstill through hand-to-hand combat.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:03.180
Yet, the threat he poses is primarily&nbsp;
in his ability to develop great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:07.200
weapons for the Decepticons, heading up&nbsp;
nefarious schemes like Project Predacon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:10.080
creating Cybermatter, and the&nbsp;
restoration of the Omega Lock.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:16.140
Grimlock is a big, scary dude with a big,&nbsp;
scary sword who can also turn into a big,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:21.480
scary T-Rex. He's a pretty solid fighter as&nbsp;
well. He leads the Dinobots, a relatively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:25.920
small team that packs a pretty nasty punch.&nbsp;
The Dinobots value strength and intensity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:29.640
so it takes an extremely powerful leader&nbsp;
to claim dominance over the rest of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:34.020
group. Grimlock has shown off his fighting&nbsp;
prowess on several occasions, and has held&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:38.601
his own against and even defeated some of a&nbsp;
veritable "Who's Who" list of Transformers.

00:07:38.601 --> 00:07:42.000
"Me Grimlock no bozo. Me king!"

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:45.660
However, he loses more often than not when&nbsp;
he tangles with any of the big timers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:48.420
and his prickly, instinctive&nbsp;
nature makes it so he often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:51.748
gets in over his head when battling&nbsp;
against physically superior foes.

00:07:51.748 --> 00:07:55.344
"Me Grimlock need new strategy."

00:07:55.344 --> 00:07:58.380
If it just came down to purely&nbsp;
physical and mental ability,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:03.120
Megatron might be able to jump a few spots on&nbsp;
this list. As the leader of the Decepticons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.800
Megatron has proven time and time again that&nbsp;
he can go toe to toe against any Transformer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:12.382
out there. He's powerful and strategic, and&nbsp;
he truly believes in what he's fighting for.

00:08:12.382 --> 00:08:17.520
That said, Megatron often fails when he should&nbsp;
succeed because his arrogance and disdain for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:22.920
others come back to haunt him. Megatron believes&nbsp;
that Transformers are the superior lifeforms in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:27.360
the universe, and any other creature that he&nbsp;
deems "inferior" is barely worth recognizing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:33.900
This arrogance has led to countless plans failing&nbsp;
due to Megatron overlooking a small detail. If he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:37.920
was able to see the big picture or recognize&nbsp;
the threat that others pose to his plans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:43.169
it's possible the Decepticons would have achieved&nbsp;
their goals of universal domination long ago.

00:08:43.169 --> 00:08:46.620
Depending on which timeline and version&nbsp;
of "Transformers" you're looking at,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:50.280
Galvatron's power level can&nbsp;
fluctuate wildly. Sometimes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:54.240
he's little more than a modified version&nbsp;
of Megatron. Other times, he has gained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:58.555
near omnipotence through a combination of&nbsp;
outside forces, cunning, and force of will.

00:08:58.555 --> 00:09:02.760
When Megatron was destroyed, he made&nbsp;
a deal with Unicron to be reborn as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:07.860
Galvatron. Though Galvatron possesses all of&nbsp;
Megatron's memories, the rebirth changed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:13.620
Decepticon forever. After his defeat by the&nbsp;
Autobots, Galvatron was driven insane. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:18.420
new quest as leader of the Decepticons was to do&nbsp;
whatever it took to gain more power for himself.

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:22.680
Galvatron's quest for domination has&nbsp;
led him to some extremely powerful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:26.340
mythical artifacts that have made him&nbsp;
almost invincible, even when battling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:31.680
the most dangerous beings in the universe. When he&nbsp;
hits his highest levels of strength, even entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:36.900
forces of the most powerful Transformers can do&nbsp;
little to stop him. Like Megatron's arrogance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:41.820
Galvatron's lust for power is his biggest&nbsp;
downfall. He will throw his companions aside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:46.920
and break ancient taboos to achieve his goals,&nbsp;
meaning almost everyone is allied against him.

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:50.184
"I am Galvatron!"

00:09:50.184 --> 00:09:53.760
Optimus Prime doesn't edge out Megatron&nbsp;
and Grimlock on battle prowess alone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:57.300
he's proven himself an extremely&nbsp;
capable fighter time and time again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:01.260
and his status as the leader of the&nbsp;
Autobots isn't a fluke. That said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:05.340
Optimus Prime's true power comes from those&nbsp;
intangible characteristics that also make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:11.000
him a good leader. He's courageous, thoughtful,&nbsp;
strategic, and never underestimates his enemies.

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:14.700
"Autobots, transform and roll out."

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:19.200
These traits help Optimus Prime stand up&nbsp;
to much more powerful forces. His drive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:22.440
and compassion help him stay in fights&nbsp;
much longer than he should be able to,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:26.400
and he often demoralizes his foes&nbsp;
simply because his will never breaks.

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:31.440
Optimus Prime is legendary in the Transformers&nbsp;
universe for turning the tide of many conflicts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:35.700
on his sheer will and courage. He has&nbsp;
sacrificed himself on countless occasions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:40.080
and taken down many a "more powerful" foe by&nbsp;
outmaneuvering them and relying on the help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:44.520
of his friends and allies. Optimus Prime&nbsp;
can never be counted out of any fight.

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:49.920
Defensor is the Combiner version of the&nbsp;
five Protectobots: Hot Spot, First Aid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:54.600
Blades, Streetwise, and Groove. He&nbsp;
isn't particularly strong on offense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.600 --> 00:11:00.060
but he does flex his power levels in other ways.&nbsp;
For one, Defensor is one of the most intelligent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:04.980
and strategic minds on any battlefield. The&nbsp;
Protectobots are all emergency responders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:09.421
so they need to be able to analyze situations&nbsp;
quickly and effectively to save lives.

00:11:09.421 --> 00:11:11.701
He's no slouch on the battlefield, certainly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.701 --> 00:11:15.420
but Defensor has one other trick&nbsp;
up his robotic sleeve: a massive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:19.620
incredibly strong force field that can be&nbsp;
projected up to 50 feet away from his body.

00:11:19.861 --> 00:11:23.461
Defensor's force field takes a&nbsp;
massive amount of energy to maintain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.461 --> 00:11:27.900
but it's an extremely powerful ability. The&nbsp;
Autobots usually get in trouble when they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:31.440
stretched too thin trying to protect&nbsp;
everyone. Defensor earns a spot on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:35.160
the list because he bypasses that weakness&nbsp;
entirely whenever he's on the battlefield.

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:41.400
Predaking is what is known as a "Combiner," which&nbsp;
is a Transformer made up of other Transformers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:45.960
As such, his power level is significant.&nbsp;
Predaking is a combination of the five other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:52.080
Predacons: Divebomb, Headstrong, Rampage,&nbsp;
Razorclaw, and Tantrum. He is massive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:56.090
extremely powerful, and one of the&nbsp;
most dangerous hunters in the galaxy.

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:59.880
Predaking also has some other abilities&nbsp;
that make him extraordinarily strong,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:03.660
but one stands out that makes&nbsp;
him unique among other Combiners.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:07.920
One of the drawbacks when a Transformer&nbsp;
shifts into its Combiner form is that all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:12.180
of them have to work together. The different&nbsp;
Transformers are still independent beings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:15.600
and if they disagree about which action&nbsp;
to take, there isn't much they can do.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:19.980
The five Transformers who become Predaking&nbsp;
mold together into one consciousness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:23.700
preventing that drawback. It makes&nbsp;
for an extremely dangerous foe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:28.740
capable of isolating and destroying his enemies.&nbsp;
Predaking's main weakness is his lust for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:32.880
hunt. He has been lured into more than a&nbsp;
few traps when he thinks he's already won.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:39.180
Bruticus is the mirror of Defensor. He's made&nbsp;
up of the five Combaticons: Onslaught, Vortex,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:44.460
Brawl, Blastoff, and Swindle. Each of these&nbsp;
Decepticons transform into military vehicles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:48.156
and when they join together, become&nbsp;
the extremely powerful Bruticus.

00:12:48.156 --> 00:12:51.600
Bruticus possesses all sorts of&nbsp;
advanced weaponry and is nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:54.480
impervious to attacks. Despite being a Combiner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:59.580
each of the five Transformers that make up this&nbsp;
monstrosity is driven by similar instincts. Thus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:03.600
it isn't very hard for them to find a common&nbsp;
purpose and work together in their Bruticus form.

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:09.300
Bruticus' central weakness is his intelligence.&nbsp;
Being driven solely by aggression makes him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:13.740
extremely suggestible and dumb. He's easy&nbsp;
to trick and will follow any orders that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:17.340
allow him to get into battle. His&nbsp;
brute strength is unquestionable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:21.300
making him a terrible threat. He just needs&nbsp;
someone else to pull the strings for him.

00:13:21.638 --> 00:13:24.928
"Not this way you traitorous oaf!"

00:13:24.928 --> 00:13:27.248
"I can't control it."

00:13:27.248 --> 00:13:33.300
If Trypticon cared a bit more, he'd be practically&nbsp;
unstoppable. He's what's known as a Titan. In one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:37.140
form, he's a massive dinosaur, capable&nbsp;
of defeating nearly any Transformer in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:42.240
hand-to-hand combat. Even worse, his alternate&nbsp;
form is a city-sized artillery platform,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:46.620
capable of launching massive amounts of&nbsp;
firepower in an incredibly short amount of time.

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:52.560
Very few can stand up to Trypticon's insane size&nbsp;
and weaponry, and entire teams of Autobots will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:57.240
generally use trickery and subversion to stand up&nbsp;
to him. They know that a head-on assault would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.240 --> 00:14:01.800
suicide. Despite being the ultimate weapon,&nbsp;
Trypticon's heart is not often in the battle.

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:07.200
Trypticon hates the Autobots, but he also hates&nbsp;
that he's used as a tool by the Decepticons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:10.920
He has accepted his role as a deadly&nbsp;
weapon, but he frequently becomes jaded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:15.060
or dispirited with the constant fighting&nbsp;
he's involved in. This disinterest is one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:18.420
of the few things that give the Autobots&nbsp;
a chance against such a dangerous foe.

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:23.202
Metroplex is an Autobot Titan, like&nbsp;
his Decepticon counterpart Trypticon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.202 --> 00:14:27.000
His alternate form is a massive city,&nbsp;
and his Autobot form is a towering,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:30.788
intimidating figure that dwarfs almost&nbsp;
any other Transformer in existence.

00:14:30.788 --> 00:14:34.688
"This planet's not big enough for the both of us!"

00:14:34.688 --> 00:14:39.660
He has three regular-sized Autobots, Scamper,&nbsp;
Six-Gun, and Slammer, just to help him keep track&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:44.220
of everything happening around him; Metroplex&nbsp;
is just too big to monitor it all himself.

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:47.580
Metroplex is a highly skilled&nbsp;
marksman and hand-to-hand fighter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:51.360
capable of scrapping with nearly&nbsp;
any foe. He's loyal, intelligent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:54.901
and courageous, and the Autobots&nbsp;
frequently rely on his judgment.

00:14:54.901 --> 00:14:59.640
Metroplex's greatest trait, however, is&nbsp;
his humility. Despite his massive size,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:04.860
fighting prowess, and intelligence, he never&nbsp;
feels it is enough. He constantly wants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:08.580
do better and improve, and he's always&nbsp;
looking for ways to overcome obstacles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:13.800
and help make the world a better place. Even&nbsp;
when the odds are against him, Metroplex is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:17.868
constantly searching for ways to even things&nbsp;
out and give the good guys the edge in battle.

00:15:18.218 --> 00:15:21.840
Omega Supreme is millions of years&nbsp;
old. He once served as the guardian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:26.340
of Cybertron's biggest city. Currently, he's&nbsp;
an intergalactic transport for the rest of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:31.738
Autobots. His alternate form is three different&nbsp;
things: a huge tank and two military bases.

00:15:31.738 --> 00:15:34.920
Omega Supreme is seemingly the&nbsp;
largest Autobot in existence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:39.420
and he is overpowered beyond belief.&nbsp;
His armor makes him invulnerable to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:42.960
all but the most powerful attacks, and&nbsp;
he has enough firepower in both of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:47.940
forms to defeat entire teams. In a one-on-one&nbsp;
fight, he would crush nearly any opposition.

00:15:48.235 --> 00:15:52.975
On top of all this, Omega Supreme has an&nbsp;
incredible drive to protect and serve.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.975 --> 00:15:57.360
He despises the destructive attitude of the&nbsp;
Decepticons and works tirelessly with Optimus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.360 --> 00:16:01.740
Prime and the other Autobots to safeguard&nbsp;
those who are in danger. Generally viewed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:05.640
as the final line of defense, he's powerful&nbsp;
enough to handle most threats on his own.

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:10.020
You could put any of the "Primes" here,&nbsp;
a group of the 13 original Transformers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.020 --> 00:16:13.800
created to become masters of different&nbsp;
aspects of the universe. Each of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:19.020
beings commands almost godlike powers, but Vector&nbsp;
Prime takes the cake for a few different reasons.

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:23.040
Vector Prime once held the Matrix of&nbsp;
Leadership, but he left Cybertron to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:27.060
become the guardian of time and space. He can&nbsp;
warp both of these things with his powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:31.320
and he can travel through and observe&nbsp;
the multiverse at will. This allows him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:35.309
to influence events across space,&nbsp;
time, and alternate dimensions.

00:16:35.309 --> 00:16:38.940
Like the rest of the Primes, Vector&nbsp;
Prime is several billion years old,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:42.900
and his existence outside of regular space and&nbsp;
time has left him with a bit of a disconnect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:47.160
from the universe. That said, his heart&nbsp;
is in the right place and there is little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:50.640
that other Transformers can do to stop&nbsp;
him once he decides on a plan of action.

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:56.160
Appearing in 2017's "Transformers: The Last&nbsp;
Knight" as one of the film's main antagonists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:56.160 --> 00:17:00.540
Quintessa is a character with the potential to&nbsp;
be the most powerful of all the Transformers.

00:17:00.754 --> 00:17:04.774
"I am Quintessa, the Prime of life."

00:17:04.774 --> 00:17:09.300
While there are plenty of claims she makes that&nbsp;
may or may not be true, she certainly was one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:13.860
the most entertaining aspects of a movie that&nbsp;
is regularly derided by fans of the franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:16.920
While the Autobots believe her to be&nbsp;
deceased after Bumblebee's attack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:21.300
the film's final sequences indicated&nbsp;
that she is alive and well, passing her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:25.534
time in human disguise, presumably&nbsp;
cooking up new nefarious schemes.

00:17:25.534 --> 00:17:30.480
Quintessa's skillset is absolutely wild, even in&nbsp;
a franchise full of immensely powerful characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:34.080
but it's easy to feel that her most&nbsp;
valuable asset is the ability to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:38.340
play the long game. While the others get&nbsp;
tangled up in battles, Quintessa tends to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:42.420
be looking to the next conflict to gauge&nbsp;
how the events will benefit her. This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:46.500
amplified by abilities like holographic&nbsp;
camouflage, hypnosis, and telekinesis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:51.360
alongside her physical attacks like energy&nbsp;
projection and redirection. However, her most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:51.360 --> 00:17:55.920
chilling talent is likely the power to transfigure&nbsp;
the Cybertronians through her power of creation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.920 --> 00:18:01.764
quite literally reverting Galvatron to Megatron&nbsp;
form to suit her needs in "The Last Knight."

00:18:01.764 --> 00:18:05.580
Most fans of "Transformers" will remember&nbsp;
Unicron's appearance in the '80s animated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:10.800
film. This godlike Transformer is the most&nbsp;
terrifying being in the universe. His entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:16.080
reason to exist is to destroy everything until&nbsp;
he is the sole remaining lifeform. He consumes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:21.176
entire worlds, breaking down everything they&nbsp;
have and using it to boost his capabilities.

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:24.060
Unicron can travel across the multiverse at will,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:28.740
and his presence is seen as a plague on&nbsp;
reality itself. His powers are unlimited,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:31.800
and he can infiltrate and infest&nbsp;
different aspects of the universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:36.960
in his never-ending quest to snuff out life.&nbsp;
He also seduces other beings under his thrall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:42.180
granting them new powers in exchange for their&nbsp;
sworn fealty. Because of the power he can bestow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:46.440
many accept his offers, despite knowing their&nbsp;
destruction always lies at the end of the deal.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:51.780
Brother to Unicron and the only being in the&nbsp;
universe who can stand up to him, Primus is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:56.100
the stand-in for God in the "Transformers"&nbsp;
universe. Primus created the Transformers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:56.100 --> 00:19:00.720
and a small part of him exists within all&nbsp;
his creations. As the Transformers create and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:05.364
maintain most other aspects of the universe,&nbsp;
Primus has his hands in nearly everything.

00:19:05.364 --> 00:19:09.060
He exists across time, space, and&nbsp;
separate realities. His physical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:13.620
manifestation exists as the Transformers'&nbsp;
home planet of Cybertron. He has access&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:18.420
to nearly all of the information in existence&nbsp;
through his mainframe computer, Vector Sigma.

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:21.420
This wealth of knowledge available&nbsp;
to Primus is what helps him edge out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:25.980
Unicron as the most powerful Transformer&nbsp;
in existence. His ability to outthink and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:29.700
strategize circles around his sibling&nbsp;
keeps the universe intact. His ability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:38.510
to exist across space and time gives&nbsp;
him the edge whenever he's needed.

